# J6 — Recon intake
# Persona: operator with an httpx export. Goal: reach recon:import.
# Known risk: flagged UNREACHABLE (BLOCKER) in the July devex audit — this
# journey exists to confirm whether an operator can get there at all.
name: Recon intake (recon:import reachability)
env: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
shell: mkdir -p @TMP_TARGET/.kuzushi && printf '[in_scope]\nhosts = ["example.com"]\n' > @TMP_TARGET/.kuzushi/scope.toml
shell: printf '{"url":"https://example.com","status_code":200,"title":"Example"}\n' > @ART/httpx.json
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 30 kuzushi>
submit: help
wait: 2
snap: help-recon-discoverability
ask: Can an operator discover recon intake from `help` at all? (July blocker: recon:import unreachable.)
submit: use recon
wait: 2
snap: use-recon
ask: `use recon` — does the module surface list an import verb with usage guidance?
submit: recon:import httpx @ART/httpx.json
wait: 8
snap: recon-import-result
expect-not: unknown tool
ask: Did recon:import actually run (materialize the export into the recon store), refuse with an ACTIONABLE error, or dead-end? Is the scope gate (scope.toml) surfaced honestly?
